{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ולקחת", :translit "ve-lakachta", :gloss "and you shall take"} {:he "בשבעה המינין", :translit "bi-shiv'ah ha-minin", :gloss "in the seven species"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ולקחת", :b "בשבעה המינין"}], :frame {:text "The verse instructs the bringing of first fruits from the produce of the land; the land of Israel is praised specifically through seven species enumerated at Deuteronomy 8:8 — wheat, barley, vines, figs, pomegranates, olive oil, and honey. By equating 'and you shall take' to 'the seven species,' the Ba'al HaTurim signals that the obligation of first fruits applies specifically to produce drawn from those seven.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 8:8" "Mishnah Bikkurim 1:3" "Mishnah Bikkurim 3:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מראשית", :translit "me-reishit", :gloss "from the beginning"} {:he "ולא כל ראשית", :translit "ve-lo kol reishit", :gloss "and not all of the beginning"} {:he "ראשית דגנך", :translit "reishit deganekha", :gloss "the first of your grain"} {:he "קדש ישראל לה' ראשית תבואתו", :translit "kodesh yisra'el la-hashem reishit tevu'ato", :gloss "Israel is holy to YHWH, the first of His produce"} {:he "ראשית ירימו חרם לה'", :translit "reishit yarimu cherm la-hashem", :gloss "the first shall raise a ban-offering to YHWH"} {:he "קטן היודע לדבר אביו מלמדו תורה", :translit "katan ha-yode'a le-daber aviv melamdo torah", :gloss "a minor who knows how to speak, his father teaches him Torah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Limmud: the word ראשית appearing here in the context of first fruits is linked to other verses that also begin with or prominently feature the word ראשית, and the legal or homiletical content of those linked verses is applied here."}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'Israel is holy to YHWH, the first of His produce' appears at Jeremiah 2:3, establishing a verbal link between the word ראשית in our first-fruits verse and the concept that Israel is God's first fruits. The obligation of a father to teach Torah to his young children is established at the beginning of the Shema verse 'and you shall teach them to your sons' (Deuteronomy 11:19), expounded in the Talmud as referring specifically to a child who has reached the age of speech (Sukkah 42a). The Ba'al HaTurim uses the repeated word ראשית to compress both homiletical and halakhic associations into the single word of this verse.", :sources ["Jeremiah 2:3" "Deuteronomy 11:19" "Sukkah 42a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ולקחת", :a-value 544, :b "בשבעה המינין", :b-value 544, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :other, :note "Limmud: the word ראשית appearing here in the context of first fruits is linked to other verses that also begin with or prominently feature the word ראשית, and the legal or homiletical content of those linked verses is applied here.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:31.654985730Z", :model "glm-5.2"}